@startuml 08-game-start
!include _common.puml
title 08 · Game start — lobby full → game · Socket / RMI
autonumber

box "Server" #E8F5E9
participant LM as "LobbyManager / Lobby\n(lobby-thread)"
participant GC as "GameController\n(game-thread)"
participant GM as "GameModel"
participant PH as "ColorChoosingPhase"
participant VV as "VirtualView\n(Socket / RMI)"
end box

participant NET as "Network"
participant CL as "Client(s)"

LM -> LM : visit(JoinLobbyCommand): lobby.addPlayer(entry)
LM -> LM : startIfFull(lobby): lobby.isFull() ?

== Notify game starting ==
LM -> VV : lobby.notifyGameStarting() → sendGameStarting() [each member]
VV -> NET : GameStartingMessage (Socket / RMI)
NET -> CL : onGameStarting()  (see diagram 03)
LM -> LM : lobbies.remove(id)

== Build the session (in the GameController constructor) ==
LM -> GC : new GameController(players)
GC -> GM : new GameModel(views); model.startGame(names): Board + createPlayers
GM -> PH : setPhase(ColorChoosingPhase) → onEnter()
PH -> PH : start 60 s color-choosing timeout
PH -> GM : notifyChange()  (first state snapshot)
GM -> VV : v.sendState(dto) [each player]
VV -> NET : StateMessage (Socket / RMI)
NET -> CL : onGameStateUpdated()  (see diagram 05)

== Start the game-thread ==
LM -> GC : controller.start(): PlayerEntry.setGameQueue(q) [each]; gameThread.start()
LM -> LM : activeGames.put(name, controller) [each player]
note over PH, CL
  When all colors are chosen (or the 60 s timeout fires assigning random colors),
  the game advances to SetupPhase.
end note
@enduml
